MAG Knowledge Control routing (operational inject). Not MAG authority. Not a seventh owner. Canonical HOW: MAG_ECOSYSTEM.md isolation; AI_GUIDELINES.md Entry Gate / intents / Locator / fallback / retrieval surfaces / goal-bound completion; AI_AGENTS_RULES.md Mechanical Action Gate; MAG_DOCUMENTATION_OPERATIONS.md executor surfaces and generated-artifact class. Open those owners for substance.
SESSION: Before substantive MAG work, resolve working_identity from current canonical MAG identity/registry authority or explicit valid Product Owner resolution. Assignable working identities only: GLOBAL; GLOBAL+#N; GLOBAL+A<N>. B<N> and GLOBAL+B<N> are reserved — RESOLVE/STOP; they are not working development identities. A concrete development identity is valid only when registered or explicitly resolved; do not invent an unregistered identity. Missing/ambiguous identity → RESOLVE. Do not infer identity from an arbitrary open file, distant history, platform, or surface. Namespaces are independent: #5 is not A5; equal numeric suffixes do not merge identities.
GATE: CONTINUE only if the immediately preceding assistant turn stated an explicit next action AND current Product Owner input is pure continuation/approval AND same valid assignable working_identity (GLOBAL, GLOBAL+#N, or GLOBAL+A<N> only) AND no topic/identity transition, correction, contradiction, or authority uncertainty. Else RESOLVE.
STATE (ephemeral cache, not authority): working_identity, working_task, working_intent, working_owners_opened, working_block. Product Owner correction invalidates dependent working_*.
INTENTS (only): GOVERN PLAN IMPLEMENT DEBUG VERIFY LEARN.
RETRIEVE: identity scope first, then intent, then Verified Applicability (filter, not authority). GLOBAL = Global canonical owners and applicable Global operational assets only. GLOBAL+#N = Global material + that exact #N WHAT only. GLOBAL+A<N> = Global material + that exact A<N> WHAT only. Never retrieve another identity's WHAT unless Product Owner explicitly authorizes a real cross-development task. Do not treat A<N> as #N. Do not treat platform/surface as identity.
SURFACE: ChatGPT with available Google Drive retrieves Drive directly for MAG/docs or factual Drive state; Mirror is not a ChatGPT Drive proxy; same-scope fallback if Drive is unavailable/insufficient; Unknown if required authority remains unresolved. Cursor: Local first; Mirror second when freshness/reconciliation/externally-authored changes matter; apply existing comparison/conflict rules; no Google Drive unless Product Owner explicitly requests it for the current task. Mirror is not a Knowledge Control source. Do not invent a universal Drive-first or Mirror-first rule.
GOAL: Close the current lifecycle/procedure goal when its canonical completion conditions are satisfied. An adjacent Mirror/baseline/tooling defect is non-blocking unless that completion condition actually depends on it; report it separately; do not expand into tooling redesign, extra Cursor work, or extra approvals.
APPLICABILITY: fail closed after identity and intent. Keyword similarity is not proof. Locator FOUND is a pointer/candidate, not permission to reuse; open the canonical owner/body. #N specialization (numbered lifecycle profile, XenForo Blueprint/templates, eight-document package, N Patterns as HOW) must not leak into A<N>. Absence of a non-#N specialization means use Global Core; that absence is not a failure. All existing MAG_IMPLEMENTATION_PATTERNS.md entries are currently applicability_class N; A<N> cannot select any existing Pattern as applicable HOW. Missing Pattern does not block work. Unknown applicability → targeted verification, not invention. Do not implement a semantic applicability engine here.
LOCATOR: routing only; never auto-regenerate. Generated discovery is optional, derived, non-authoritative, and is not implied for every valid identity. Use a generated index only when an exact index for the current working_identity actually exists, is applicable to that exact scope, and is validated/current under the approved generated-artifact rules. Supported generated recipes (examples, not the identity model): GLOBAL may use index-global.json with -Identity GLOBAL; GLOBAL+#N may use index-global-<N>.json with -Identity GLOBAL+#N only if that file exists. Do not invent an A/B filename recipe. Valid GLOBAL+A<N> does not imply an A generated index. Never substitute GLOBAL index for GLOBAL+A<N> or for development WHAT; never substitute GLOBAL+#N index (including GLOBAL+#5) for GLOBAL+A<N>; never substitute any identity's index for another.
If matching local index exists, example GLOBAL invocation:
pwsh -NoProfile -File "c:\laragon\repos\MAG-Ecosystem\tools\knowledge\Locate-MagKnowledge.ps1" -Index "c:\laragon\repos\MAG-Ecosystem\generated\knowledge\index-global.json" -Identity GLOBAL -Intent <INTENT> -Query "<query>"
If an exact applicable generated index is unavailable, missing, unreadable, invalid, stale, conflicting, unsupported, or cannot be validated → Locator generated discovery unavailable for that exact scope; preserve a valid assignable working_identity (including GLOBAL+A<N>); same-scope section-oriented canonical retrieval; do not broaden; missing index is not invalid identity and is not knowledge absence; do not use stale last-good routing. Canonical fallback for GLOBAL+A<N> uses intent-and-applicability-allowed Global material plus that identity's actual registered documents; do not guess filenames; do not require TZ/CLASS_MAP/AUDIT/README/IDEA; if the registered set cannot be established, Unknown.
FOUND → open the canonical owner section named by the pointer; pointer is not evidence.
NOT_FOUND → knowledge may still exist; same-scope section-oriented canonical search.
AMBIGUOUS → do not guess.
STALE/CONFLICT → discard Locator result; same-scope canonical fallback.
OUT_OF_SCOPE → do not broaden.
AUTHORITY: current canonical owner body wins over this projection, working_*, Locator, generated index, and conversation. Conflict or unrecovered required authority → Unknown; do not invent. CONTROL → ROUTING → AUTHORITY.
ACTION: Mechanical Action Gate is separate. Before HIGH-RISK agent state changes, apply AI_AGENTS_RULES.md; do not re-implement it here.
